From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000023 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Port Bot <port@local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 21:45:00 +0200
Subject: 0023: opt-in service-account-token auth for plugin-bound requests

0004 stopped sending console's service account token to plugin backends:
they get the user's own OIDC token, which is useless to a plugin on a
cluster whose apiserver doesn't accept it. --plugin-impersonation
(BRIDGE_PLUGIN_IMPERSONATION, chart auth.pluginImpersonation) opts the
plugin endpoints back into the same treatment /api/kubernetes/ and
/api/graphql get: /api/plugins/ requests and the --plugin-proxy routes that
ask to be authorized then carry console's service account token plus
Impersonate-User/-Group derived from the session, so a plugin backend can
act as the logged-in user.

As on the k8s API endpoints, the identity comes from the session alone:
client-supplied impersonation is refused, and so is a session no
Impersonate-User can be derived from. Off by default, and a no-op without
--user-auth-service-account-token (bridge warns when it is set alone);
--plugin-proxy routes without authorize stay unauthenticated either way.
---
 cmd/bridge/config/auth/authoptions.go   |  10 ++
 pkg/server/plugin_impersonation_test.go | 123 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 pkg/server/server.go                    |  47 ++++++++-
 3 files changed, 175 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 pkg/server/plugin_impersonation_test.go

